      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona Alpine Resort 15 August 2026 — Cardrona is expecting a mainly fine morning with some low cloud before a front arrives this afternoon, bringing snow showers and moderate westerly winds. It will be a cold day, with the freezing level dropping, so warm clothing is recommended. All trails were groomed overnight and will start firm before gradually releasing through the day. Off-trail snow is expected to remain firm, so caution is advised. Learners Slope, Main Basin, Captains and Soho are open, while Mt Cardrona is on hold. Ski Touring Access is also open. Main Basin lifts are scheduled from 8:30am, with Captains, T-Bar, Soho and Willows following from 9:00am. Big Bucks is on hold in the terrain park. An active road hazard advisory is in place for the Cardrona access road. Chains must be carried and may need to be fitted later as conditions change. The resort also notes muddy sections as the road thaws. The resort is currently showing 5 of 6 car parks open, with Carpark A full and the other listed parking areas available.",
