      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 15 August 2026 — Start the weekend on freshly groomed pistes, with the groomers reported in excellent shape and plenty of terrain available across Home and Saddle Basins. Conditions are currently cold with low visibility moving in from the south, while the mountain is expecting the possibility of a few centimetres of fresh snow later. The Saddle Basin offers natural alpine terrain, while Summit Slopes remain on hold. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Groomed terrain including Triple Treat, Beginner Platter, Main Street, Big Skite, Rafill's Run, Pete's Treat, High Street, Bullet, Saddle Track, Saddleback and Roller Coaster is open. Summit Slopes are on hold, while Matukituki Basin, Motatapu Chutes and Sundance remain closed. All vehicles must carry chains, and the resort recommends using the free road shuttle. The Rise & Shine Race 2 pre-dawn skinning race is scheduled for tomorrow.",
